        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:01 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Verizon Maryland Inc.",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1531",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "614304228dbf3b9cc1d4b243f27009575297363685d00018c64974d807d22f49",
      "evidence_id": "ev-614304228dbf-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Unlike Mr. Smith, Verizon takes the position that these contracts are, in fact, pervasive and Federal, and I'd like to tell you why. The statute, by its terms, requires us to enter into these relationships whether we want to or not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1531",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "document_hash": "614304228dbf3b9cc1d4b243f27009575297363685d00018c64974d807d22f49",
      "evidence_id": "ev-614304228dbf-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: 252(a)(1)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1531",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "614304228dbf3b9cc1d4b243f27009575297363685d00018c64974d807d22f49",
      "evidence_id": "ev-614304228dbf-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Initially, I'd like to note that although this -- in this case the Court granted certiorari only on the question of jurisdiction under section 1331,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1531",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "614304228dbf3b9cc1d4b243f27009575297363685d00018c64974d807d22f49",
      "evidence_id": "ev-614304228dbf-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But I think you're -- aren't you positing a system in which there -- I was going to say, aren't you positing a system in which, as a system, we assume there is going to be some kind of a system of utility regulation, and there isn't going to be a system."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Fourth Circuit",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1531",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "614304228dbf3b9cc1d4b243f27009575297363685d00018c64974d807d22f49",
      "evidence_id": "ev-614304228dbf-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, the Fourth Circuit dismissed the 1331 claim on the basis of three alternative grounds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1531",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "614304228dbf3b9cc1d4b243f27009575297363685d00018c64974d807d22f49",
      "evidence_id": "ev-614304228dbf-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: So you say that what has been created is this weird system in which challenges to the interpretation or validity of negotiated agreements can't go to Federal court, but if it's a challenge to an arbitrated agreement, it does go to Federal court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Miller",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1531",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "614304228dbf3b9cc1d4b243f27009575297363685d00018c64974d807d22f49",
      "evidence_id": "ev-614304228dbf-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MILLER: I don't know that it's so in any -- in every instance. In this instance, for a matter of fact, the initial contract at issue with MFS and Telenet, Verizon actually agreed to a reciprocal compensation rate that was higher than the commission's arbitrated rate. Now, for what reason, I don't know. Presumably they traded something else for that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1531",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "614304228dbf3b9cc1d4b243f27009575297363685d00018c64974d807d22f49",
      "evidence_id": "ev-614304228dbf-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The whole case was dismissed."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
